NOTE: Make sure you have development files for gtk1.3 or better before 
compiling.  This includes associated packages like Pango.

Type "make" to compile xpad.

Type "make install" as root to install the binary to /usr/local/bin.  Or, just
copy the file to your path directory of choice.

If you are upgrading from an earlier version of xpad (pre 0.2), your old notes
will not be recognized by xpad 0.2.  You may delete the old windows* files in
~/.xpad/.

